                %use{:x => "83.902", "xlink:href" => "#inWUuc2Ee54YQLI3qfOzBMXfcGI=-glyph-4-2", :y => "11.713"}
              %g{:fill => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "fill-opacity" => "1"}
                %use{:x => "85.8", "xlink:href" => "#inWUuc2Ee54YQLI3qfOzBMXfcGI=-glyph-1-2", :y => "52.212"}
              %g{:fill => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "fill-opacity" => "1"}
                %use{:x => "82.811", "xlink:href" => "#inWUuc2Ee54YQLI3qfOzBMXfcGI=-glyph-2-3", :y => "78.964"}
              %g{:fill => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "fill-opacity" => "1"}
                %use{:x => "82.811", "xlink:href" => "#inWUuc2Ee54YQLI3qfOzBMXfcGI=-glyph-3-3", :y => "78.964"}
              %path{:d => "M 77.3355 -5.977062 L 77.3355 -65.902844 ", :fill => "none", :stroke => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "stroke-linecap" => "round", "stroke-linejoin" => "round", "stroke-miterlimit" => "10", "stroke-opacity" => "1", "stroke-width" => "0.478", :transform => "matrix(1, 0, 0, -1, 5.477, 13.062)"}
              %g{:fill => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "fill-opacity" => "1"}
                %use{:x => "72.473", "xlink:href" => "#inWUuc2Ee54YQLI3qfOzBMXfcGI=-glyph-0-2", :y => "90.919"}
              %g{:fill => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "fill-opacity" => "1"}
                %use{:x => "77.899", "xlink:href" => "#inWUuc2Ee54YQLI3qfOzBMXfcGI=-glyph-5-1", :y => "90.919"}
              %g{:fill => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "fill-opacity" => "1"}
                %use{:x => "82.451", "xlink:href" => "#inWUuc2Ee54YQLI3qfOzBMXfcGI=-glyph-0-3", :y => "90.919"}
              %g{:fill => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "fill-opacity" => "1"}
                %use{:x => "88.596", "xlink:href" => "#inWUuc2Ee54YQLI3qfOzBMXfcGI=-glyph-5-2", :y => "90.919"}
            %p
              we see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(\beta)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(\alpha\circ\beta)
              must lift to morphisms with identical domains, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(\beta)
              has domain
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(b)
            %p
              Functoriality now follows easily from uniqueness of lifting for a discrete fibration, and it is not hard to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              is a solution to the lifting problem.
          %p
            Dually, there is an orthogonal factorisation system
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,M)
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            for which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is the class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+functors"} initial functors
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is the class of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+opfibrations"} discrete opfibrations
          %h2#remark_on_the_terminology Remark on the terminology
          %p
            Under the functorial reformulation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+separation"} axiom of comprehension
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"} Lawvere
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lawvere70"}> 1970
            ) the comprehensive factorization can be viewed as a generalization of the epi-mono factorization of a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
            occurring in the context of set-theoretic comprehension: the best approximation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            by a property in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^Y
            (i.e.
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mrow
                        %mi im
                        %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_{im f}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi im
                    %mi f
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} im f\hookrightarrow Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo :
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi K
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:\int K\to D
            given by the factorization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %mi m
                  %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F=m{}e
            can be viewed as the “extension” of the approximation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            by the “property”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{D}
          %p
            More generally, instances of the comprehension scheme correspond to factorization systems (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Bergkauf"} Berger-Kaufmann
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+separation"} comprehension scheme
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+F.+C.+Walters"} R. F. C. Walters
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Comprehensive Factorization of a Functor
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/bulletin-of-the-american-mathematical-society-new-series/volume-79/issue-5/The-comprehensive-factorization-of-a-functor/bams/1183534973.full"} bams:1183534973
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9904-1973-13268-9"} doi:10.1090/S0002-9904-1973-13268-9
          %p Note there is a mistake in the proof of the main theorem of the paper above, as noted on page 74 of:
          %ul
            %li#Kelly82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"}> Max Kelly
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Basic concepts of enriched category theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 64
                %strong 10
                (2005) 1-136 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/de/academic/subjects/mathematics/logic-categories-and-sets/basic-concepts-enriched-category-theory?format=PB&isbn=9780521287029"}> ISBN:9780521287029
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/10/tr10abs.html"} tac:tr10
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/10/tr10.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Lawvere70
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere"}> Lawvere
                , F. W.
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Equality in hyperdoctrines and comprehension schema as an adjoint functor
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Proc. New York Symp. on Applications of Categorical Algebra
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/LawvereComprehension.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fosco+Loregian"}> Fosco Loregian
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"} Emily Riehl
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorical Notions of Fibration
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 38
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.06129"} arXiv:1806.06129
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.exmath.2019.02.004"} doi:10.1016/j.exmath.2019.02.004
            %li{:id => "BergKauf]"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clemens+Berger"}> Clemens Berger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+M.+Kaufmann"} Ralph M. Kaufmann
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Comprehensive Factorization Systems
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/tbilisi-mathematical-journal/volume-10/issue-3/Comprehensive-factorisation-systems/10.1515/tmj-2017-0112.short"} doi:10.1515/tmj-2017-0112
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Perrone"}> Paolo Perrone
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kan extensions are partial colimits
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 30
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.04531"} arXiv:2101.04531
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-021-09671-9"} doi:10.1007/s10485-021-09671-9
          %p
            Internal comprehensive factorisations (and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsors"} torsors
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Verity"} Dominic Verity
              = succeed "," do
                %em The comprehensive factorization and torsors
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TAC"} TAC
              %strong 23
              (2010) 42-75 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/23/3/23-03abs.html"}> tac:23-03
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A generalisation to a bicategorical factorization system on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CAT
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAT
            is considered in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Variation on a Comprehensive Theme
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TAC"} TAC
              %strong 37
              (2021) 964-978 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/37/29/37-29.pdf"}> tac:37-29
              \&amp;rbrack;
